# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# Why this matters for this project specifically: the published package's SHA-256
# is recorded in artifacts/SHA256SUMS.txt, and line endings change file bytes.
# Without this, the same commit checked out on Windows and on Linux produces
# different archives, so the checksum a reviewer downloads cannot be compared to
# the one the build printed.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` stores LF in the repository and checks out LF everywhere.
# Windows editors still show and save CRLF correctly; git normalises on commit.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated and vendored data must never be rewritten: byte-for-byte
# reproducibility of the Public Suffix List is what makes its hash meaningful.
vendor/public_suffix_list.dat -text
src/generated/psl.json -text

# Binary assets.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary

# Lockfiles are diffed line by line and must stay text.
package-lock.json text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must stay LF or they break on Unix.
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
